      <h2>2. Hosting and server log files</h2>
      <p>This website is hosted by <strong>Netlify, Inc., 101 2nd Street, San Francisco, CA 94105, USA</strong> and delivered via its worldwide content delivery network (CDN). Every visit to the website is therefore processed on Netlify servers, which may also be located outside the EU. Transfer to the USA is based on the EU–US Data Privacy Framework, under which Netlify is certified, and on the EU Standard Contractual Clauses.</p>
      <p>Each time our website is accessed, Netlify automatically collects the following technical information in server log files: IP address of the requesting device, date and time of access, URL accessed, data volume transferred, HTTP status code, browser and operating system used, and the referrer URL where applicable.</p>
      <p>These data are technically necessary to deliver the website and are used to detect and defend against attacks. No merging with other data sources takes place. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in the secure and stable provision of the website). We do not analyse or separately store the log files ourselves; their retention period is determined by Netlify.</p>

